 "drivingQuestion": "Why is a bell on the slave's clothes permitted if the neck bell is forbidden lest it break?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "the clothing bell is woven in, so no decree",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "shabbat.58a.15",
   "daf": "58a",
   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "אָמַר מָר: וְלֹא בְּזוֹג שֶׁבְּצַוָּארוֹ, אֲבָל יוֹצֵא הוּא בְּזוֹג שֶׁבִּכְסוּתוֹ.",
   "en": "In that same baraita «the Master said» that the slave may «not» go out «with a bell that is around his neck, but he may go out with a bell that is on his clothes.»"
  },
  {
   "id": "shabbat.58a.16",
   "daf": "58a",
   "sentenceId": 15,
   "he": "זוֹג שֶׁבְּצַוָּארוֹ אַמַּאי לָא — דִּילְמָא מִיפְּסִיק וְאָתֵי לְאֵיתוֹיֵי? זוֹג שֶׁבִּכְסוּתוֹ נָמֵי לִיחוּשׁ דִּילְמָא מִיפְּסִיק וְאָתֵי לְאֵיתוֹיֵי!",
   "en": "The Gemara asks: With «a bell that is around his neck, why» may he «not» go out? It is due to concern «lest it be severed and he come to carry it.» If so, with «a bell on his clothes too, let us be concerned lest it be severed and he come to carry it.»"
  },
  {
   "id": "shabbat.58a.17",
   "daf": "58a",
   "sentenceId": 16,
   "he": "הָכָא בְמַאי עָסְקִינַן — דִּימְחָא בֵּיהּ מוּמְחָא. וְכִדְרַב הוּנָא בְּרֵיהּ דְּרַב יְהוֹשֻׁעַ. דְּאָמַר רַב הוּנָא בְּרֵיהּ דְּרַב יְהוֹשֻׁעַ: כׇּל שֶׁהוּא אָרוּג לֹא גָּזְרוּ.",
   "en": "The Gemara answers: «With what are we dealing here?» With a case «where» the bell «is woven into» the garment, «and» it is «in accordance with» the opinion of «Rav Huna, son of Rav Yehoshua, as Rav Huna, son of Rav Yehoshua, said:» A«nything that is woven» into a garment, «the Sages did not issue a decree» prohibiting going out with it on Shabbat."
  }
 ],
